# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ⚠  SPICYQUOTE NOTICE — every secret in this file was BLANKED before it was
#    committed. The upstream copy that arrived in SpicyTool-main.zip carried
#    live credentials (a Flybasis Supabase anon key, a refresh token, the owner
#    PIN and the owner's login e-mails). They have been replaced with empty
#    values; fill them in from your own Vercel/1Password secrets, never here.
#
#    The same capture that leaked them (agentsearch.vercel.app.har) has been
#    deleted from this vendored copy.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SpicyTool — PRODUCTION environment (Vercel)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This file is READY to import into Vercel:
#   Vercel project -> Settings -> Environment Variables -> paste / bulk-add ->
#   tick Production (+ Preview) -> Save -> Redeploy.
#
# NOTES (read before uploading):
#   * `FLYBASIS_*` values below are the MAIN Flybasis award-feed token for this
#     deployment, captured from a real Flybasis login in
#     agentsearch.vercel.app.har. Treat them as the primary persistent
#     credential, not a throwaway.
#   * `.env.example` is a TRACKED file. If this repo is PUBLIC, do not commit
#     these secrets here — paste the file into Vercel and then blank/delete
#     the FLYBASIS_SUPABASE_* lines before committing. Keep them only in
#     Vercel's Environment Variables or a git-ignored `.env`.
#   * Only the live providers are listed. PointsYeah / Seats.Aero / AwardTool
#     and the modeled engine are intentionally excluded from the production
#     set: the award feed is Flybasis alone.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Owner PIN login ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Two-step PIN sign-in. These match the built-in defaults so nothing changes
# silently; keep them here so Vercel uses explicit values you can audit.
ALLOWED_LOGIN_EMAILS=you@example.com
LOGIN_PIN=
# Strong random value (64+ chars) so sessions survive cold starts with a real
# secret instead of the derived fallback. Generate one, e.g.:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
# and set it ONLY in Vercel / your private .env — never in this file.
# AUTH_SECRET=

# ── Flybasis award feed (the ONLY provider searched by default) ─────────────
# MAIN TOKEN — this is the live Flybasis credential the app authenticates with.
# The Supabase anon key + refresh token below were captured from the account's
# real email-OTP login (agentsearch.vercel.app.har) and are used together as
# the primary, persistent award-feed credential for this deployment.
#
#   * FLYBASIS_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY  = Supabase "apikey" (public client key) — the
#     fixed identifier for the sb.flybasis.com project; stable across logins.
#   * FLYBASIS_REFRESH_TOKEN      = the account's refresh token — the durable
#     credential that re-authenticates the award socket on every request.
#     (Supabase here issues short opaque tokens, e.g. 14 chars — normal.)
#   * FLYBASIS_EMAIL              = the account this token belongs to.
#
# These are treated as the main token for production, not a throwaway. They do
# NOT expire on a timer, and no other instance is rotating them in this setup.
# Keep this pair consistent (anon key + its matching refresh token) and the
# award feed stays live. If you ever sign in again on the Flybasis site with
# this account, or paste in a different token, update BOTH lines together from
# that same login.
#
# Alternative MAIN token — an OFFICIAL Flybasis award-feed API key
# (https://flybasis.com; issued for enterprise-api.flybasis.com, see
# https://flybasis.github.io/searchapi.docs). If you set FLYBASIS_API_KEY, the
# app uses it and ignores the session pair below. It is NOT a RapidAPI key.
FLYBASIS_API_KEY=
# Award socket host override (staging/local mocks only; leave unset in prod):
# FLYBASIS_BASE_URL=https://enterprise-api.flybasis.com

# Which providers the search relays. Production = Flybasis only.
SPICYTOOL_PROVIDERS=Flybasis

# Off so searches only ever show real provider results (never modeled data).
SPICYTOOL_MODELED_ENGINE=0

# ── Flybasis session (the main award-feed token) ────────────────────────────
FLYBASIS_SUPABASE_URL=https://sb.flybasis.com
FLYBASIS_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
FLYBASIS_REFRESH_TOKEN=
FLYBASIS_EMAIL=

# ── AgentSearch (RapidAPI) — OPTIONAL web context only ──────────────────────
# Backs the "Web context" panel (general web pages — never award data). When
# unset the keyless MCP connector below is the fallback.
# Get a key at rapidapi.com (AgentSearch API).
AGENTSEARCH_API_KEY=
AGENTSEARCH_PROVIDER=brave
AGENTSEARCH_COUNTRY=us
AGENTSEARCH_TIMEOUT=12
# Optional MCP fallback (keyless). Same 3-tool surface as the keyless connector.
# AGENTSEARCH_MCP_URL=https://agentsearch-mcp.vercel.app/mcp

# ── FlyBasis Search MCP connector — OPTIONAL web context fallback ───────────
# Supplies the "Web context" panel when AgentSearch is unset. Keyless, so the
# default URL needs no credential. Leave blank/unset and the panel just reports
# unavailable.
FLYBASIS_MCP_URL=https://flybasis-mcp.vercel.app/mcp
FLYBASIS_MCP_TIMEOUT=12

# ── Cache / engine tuning ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Vercel injects VERCEL=1 automatically; with no REDIS_URL the cache uses the
# built-in per-instance memory store (no sidecar required). Set REDIS_URL only
# if you run an external Redis (Upstash/Vercel KV-compatible URL).
# REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379/0
CACHE_TTL=2700
PROVIDER_TIMEOUT=3.5
